omen-vote-hint = The whole party decides. A tie is settled by lot.
omen-well = The Well
omen-well-text = The frame has gone black and the bucket is dry, though the chain is wet to the windlass. Below, someone counts under their breath, and loses count exactly at your number.
omen-well-look = Look into the water
omen-well-pass = Walk past
omen-crossroads_stone = The Stone at the Crossroads
omen-crossroads_stone-text = Three notches on the stone and not one letter. The moss was scraped off it lately. By fingernails. From the inside.
omen-crossroads_stone-left = Left
omen-crossroads_stone-right = Right
omen-crossroads_stone-straight = Straight on
omen-hungry_village = The Hungry Village
omen-hungry_village-text = The stoves are lit and no smoke rises. The children stand by the fence and look not at you but at your packs. One holds a spoon. It has been clean a long time.
omen-hungry_village-give = Give them your supplies
omen-hungry_village-steal = Rob an empty hut
omen-hungry_village-pass = Leave before dark
omen-bannik = The Bannik in the Bathhouse
omen-bannik-text = The bathhouse is hot, though its owners were buried in autumn. Something turns over on the top bench and asks for more steam. The third steam is his; everyone knows that.
omen-bannik-steam = Bathe in the first steam
omen-bannik-pay = Leave him a coin on the bench
omen-bannik-leave = Do not go in
omen-drowned_mill = The Drowned Mill
omen-drowned_mill-text = The wheel stands still and the stones turn. The flour on the floor is damp and grey, and the footprints in it are bare and small and all go one way: to the water.
omen-drowned_mill-search = Search the bin
omen-drowned_mill-grind = Take a turn at the stone
omen-hanged_man = The Hanged Man on the Oak
omen-hanged_man-text = He has hung a long while; his bast shoes have worn out on the air. As you come near he stops swinging and says evenly, without malice: "Ask. One at a time."
omen-hanged_man-listen = Hear him out
omen-hanged_man-cut_down = Cut him down and search him
omen-hanged_man-flee = Leave without looking back
omen-hen_legged_hut = The Hut on Hen's Legs
omen-hen_legged_hut-text = The hut stands with its back to the forest and shifts its feet when it thinks no one is looking. The door is open just wide enough for a hand.
omen-hen_legged_hut-enter = Go in
omen-hen_legged_hut-knock = Knock and wait
omen-rusalka_pool = The Rusalka's Pool
omen-rusalka_pool-text = The water is warm as a bathhouse and smells of apples. A shirt is drying on a branch over the pool. It is dry. It has been drying for three years.
omen-rusalka_pool-drink = Drink your fill
omen-rusalka_pool-leave = Go round by the bank

