battle-tutorial = Drag a card onto an enemy or a hero; a card with no target, up onto the field. Above each enemy is what it will do, and to whom. When your turn is done, press Ready. Hover a unit and press 1-5 to signal the party.

omen-wedding_of_the_dead = The Wedding of the Dead
omen-wedding_of_the_dead-text = Tables are laid in the open field; the guests sit straight and do not eat. The groom turns his head, only his head, and shifts along the bench: sit.
omen-wedding_of_the_dead-sit = Sit at the table
omen-wedding_of_the_dead-dance = Dance with the bride
omen-wedding_of_the_dead-refuse = Refuse
omen-kurgan = The Barrow
omen-kurgan-text = The mound is breathing. The grass on it lies down and rises evenly, like a sleeper's chest. At its foot, a fresh pit and someone's spade.
omen-kurgan-dig = Dig on
omen-kurgan-bow = Bow and leave
omen-kurgan-pass = Go round
omen-ferryman = The Ferryman
omen-ferryman-text = He rows without looking at the water. The boat is damp with other people's tears. "A coin under the tongue," he says, "or wade. Waders arrive too. Some."
omen-ferryman-pay = Pay
omen-ferryman-wade = Wade across
omen-talking_cat = The Cat on the Chain
omen-talking_cat-text = The cat paces its chain around a stump, speaking low, like a bookkeeper. It knows which of your cards is one too many. It knows something else as well.
omen-talking_cat-listen = Listen
omen-talking_cat-feed = Feed it
omen-talking_cat-shoo = Shoo it off
omen-crying_child = Crying in the Windfall
omen-crying_child-text = A child is crying. It has cried long and evenly, never drawing breath. Under a spruce lies a bundle, far heavier than it should be.
omen-crying_child-comfort = Pick it up
omen-crying_child-walk_on = Walk on
omen-smithy_ruin = The Dead Smithy
omen-smithy_ruin-text = The forge is cold and the bellows are working. On the anvil lies a shoe for a hoof no horse has.
omen-smithy_ruin-forge = Blow up the forge
omen-smithy_ruin-scavenge = Gather the iron
omen-leshy_trail = Led by the Leshy
omen-leshy_trail-text = The same pine for the third time, with your own notch on it. Only the notch is higher now, as if the tree had been growing while you walked.
omen-leshy_trail-follow = Follow him
omen-leshy_trail-turn_coats = Turn your coats inside out
omen-leshy_trail-wait = Wait for light
omen-bog_lights = The Lights
omen-bog_lights-text = They burn over the causeway in pairs, at eye height. When you stop, they stop. When you blink, there is one more.
omen-bog_lights-chase = Go toward them
omen-bog_lights-ignore = Watch your feet
omen-old_shrine = The Old Shrine
omen-old_shrine-text = The idols are set facing into the ring. The mouth of the end one is smeared with something fresh. It alone faces outward, and it was not you who turned it.
omen-old_shrine-offer = Leave an offering
omen-old_shrine-pray = Pray
omen-old_shrine-desecrate = Strip it bare
omen-frozen_host = The Frozen Host
omen-frozen_host-text = They stand in ranks on the ice with their spears, and the frost on their beards does not melt. The end man holds a letter. The seal is whole. The name on it is one of yours.
omen-frozen_host-loot = Search them
omen-frozen_host-bury = Bury them properly
omen-frozen_host-leave = Leave them be
omen-pedlar_ghost = The Faceless Pedlar
omen-pedlar_ghost-text = His box is the same, only nothing looks out of the cracks any more. He lays his wares on the snow and waits. He gives change in earth.
omen-pedlar_ghost-trade = Buy
omen-pedlar_ghost-haggle = Haggle
omen-pedlar_ghost-decline = Decline
omen-bone_mill = The Bone Mill
omen-bone_mill-text = It grinds with no wind and no water. The flour comes white, fine and warm. The miller offers to grind yours too: whatever you no longer need.
omen-bone_mill-grind = Give it to the stones
omen-bone_mill-rest = Warm yourself by the stones

