omen-krada-burn = Cast something of yours into the fire
omen-krada-refuse = Keep away
omen-krada = The Pyre
omen-krada-text = A funeral pyre stands in the clearing with no body upon it. The wood is dry, the flame steady. It is waiting, and it does not tire of waiting.
omen-blood_oak-feed = Lay a palm against the bark
omen-blood_oak-refuse = Go around
omen-blood_oak = The Thirsty Oak
omen-blood_oak-text = The bark at the roots is dark and sticky. The oak rustles with no wind, and one word in the rustling is plain: give.
omen-forked_path-left = Follow the drag marks
omen-forked_path-right = Into the raspberry thicket
omen-forked_path = The Fork
omen-forked_path-text = The trail has split where yesterday it was one. To the left something heavy was dragged not long ago. To the right it smells of raspberries, out of season.
omen-wolf_shepherd-tribute = Pay him off
omen-wolf_shepherd-defy = Take his staff from him
omen-wolf_shepherd-bow = Bow and pass
omen-wolf_shepherd = The Wolf Shepherd
omen-wolf_shepherd-text = An old man in a grey sheepskin sits on a stump with wolves lying meek around him. He counts your heads the way one counts sheep.
omen-mushroom_ring-step = Step into the ring
omen-mushroom_ring-pick = Pick mushrooms from the edge
omen-mushroom_ring-skirt = Walk around it
omen-mushroom_ring = The Witch Ring
omen-mushroom_ring-text = Toadstools stand in a clean ring. The grass inside lies flat, as if there had been dancing there that stopped when you stepped out of the trees.
omen-bee_tree-reach = Reach into the hollow
omen-bee_tree-smoke = Smoke it out and gather
omen-bee_tree-leave = Leave it be
omen-bee_tree = The Bee Tree
omen-bee_tree-text = The hollow hums, yet no bees show. Honey runs down the trunk black, and not one fly hangs over it.
omen-lost_hunter-share = Give him your warmth
omen-lost_hunter-refuse = Pass in silence
omen-lost_hunter = The Lost Hunter
omen-lost_hunter-text = He says he has been lost three days. His beard has grown three years. He asks only for bread and a little of someone's warmth.
omen-owl_omen-follow = Follow the owl
omen-owl_omen-wait = Wait for dusk
omen-owl_omen = An Owl by Day
omen-owl_omen-text = An owl sits on a bough in broad daylight, unblinking. Then it lifts off and flies slowly, so that one may keep up.
omen-hollow_log-crawl = Crawl in
omen-hollow_log-pass = Walk past
omen-hollow_log = The Hollow Log
omen-hollow_log-text = Something glints inside the fallen trunk. The way in is narrow, and warm air comes out of it as from a mouth.
omen-two_bridges-bridge = Over the bridge
omen-two_bridges-ford = By the ford
omen-two_bridges = The Plank and the Ford
omen-two_bridges-text = A rotten plank bridge crosses the gully, and downstream there is a ford. On the far bank, under the bridge, someone has left a bundle.
omen-charcoal_burner-temper = Hand him your weapon
omen-charcoal_burner-sit = Warm yourself by the pit
omen-charcoal_burner-leave = Leave
omen-charcoal_burner = The Charcoal Burner
omen-charcoal_burner-text = He does not turn and does not stop raking the pit. "Iron is tempered while it is hot. So are people." You never do see his face.
omen-empty_cradle-rock = Rock it and sing
omen-empty_cradle-leave = Leave the hut
omen-empty_cradle = The Empty Cradle
omen-empty_cradle-text = In a roofless hut a cradle swings. It is empty, yet it creaks as though it bore a weight. Someone must rock it while the others go by.
omen-plague_cart-pull = Take the shafts
omen-plague_cart-aside = Squeeze past
omen-plague_cart = The Plague Cart
omen-plague_cart-text = A cart stands across the street, its shafts empty. Under the sacking lie the goods of those who no longer need them. It will not move by itself.
omen-church_and_tavern-chapel = Into the chapel
omen-church_and_tavern-tavern = Into the tavern
omen-church_and_tavern = The Chapel and the Tavern
omen-church_and_tavern-text = They stand door to door. One candle burns in the chapel; in the tavern, all of them. In both, it seems, you were expected.
omen-gallows_crows-feed = Feed the flock
omen-gallows_crows-scare = Scatter them and take the ring
omen-gallows_crows-go = Leave without looking back
omen-gallows_crows = The Court of Crows
omen-gallows_crows-text = The gallows hangs empty, yet the crows sit in rows as at a moot. The eldest drops a stranger's ring at your feet and waits for an answer.
omen-drowned_bell-ring = Pull the rope
omen-drowned_bell-dive = Dive for the silver
omen-drowned_bell-listen = Hear it out and go
omen-drowned_bell = The Drowned Bell
omen-drowned_bell-text = The belfry has sunk into the bog up to its cross. Under the water the bell tolls by itself: dull, slow, and each time a little nearer.
omen-widow_bread-eat = Break off a piece
omen-widow_bread-pay = Leave a coin and eat it all
omen-widow_bread-refuse = Thank her and go
omen-widow_bread = The Widow's Bread
omen-widow_bread-text = A warm loaf lies on the table. The woman kneads the next and does not look up. There is no flour in the house, and the stove is cold.
omen-swamp_fork-causeway = Along the causeway
omen-swamp_fork-reeds = Toward the voice
omen-swamp_fork = The Causeway and the Reeds
omen-swamp_fork-text = The log causeway runs straight, with something spilled along it. In the reeds a low voice is calling a name: not everyone's, only one.
omen-black_rooster-buy = Pay for everyone
omen-black_rooster-no = Decline
omen-black_rooster = The Black Rooster
omen-black_rooster-text = A woman on a porch holds a black rooster. "When he crows, every unclean thing for a mile goes quiet. But he does not crow for nothing."
omen-cellar_door-down = Go down
omen-cellar_door-nail = Nail it shut and search the hut
omen-cellar_door = The Cellar
omen-cellar_door-text = The cellar hatch is braced from within. Something scratches below: careful, patient, one nail along the same board.
omen-mirror_house-break = Smash the mirrors
omen-mirror_house-cover = Cover them, as is proper
omen-mirror_house-look = Turn around
omen-mirror_house = The House of Mirrors
omen-mirror_house-text = In the dead man's house not one mirror was covered. Each shows you, and one more who stands a little behind.
omen-river_smorodina-toll = Wade in first
omen-river_smorodina-back = Look for another way
omen-river_smorodina = The River Smorodina
omen-river_smorodina-text = Its water burns and gives no warmth. There is no ferry. The river lets all pass if one leaves it a part of themselves, for good.
omen-kalinov_bridge-over = Across the bridge
omen-kalinov_bridge-under = Under the bridge
omen-kalinov_bridge = The Kalinov Bridge
omen-kalinov_bridge-text = The bridge glows red-hot. Beneath it runs a path over the bones of those who would not cross above. Both ways lead to the far side.
omen-ancestors_table-sit = Sit and share the meal
omen-ancestors_table-bread = Take bread for the road
omen-ancestors_table-bow = Ask their blessing
omen-ancestors_table = The Ancestors' Table
omen-ancestors_table-text = The table is laid for all of you and many more. Those seated neither eat nor speak. Beside each of them one place stands empty.
omen-nameless_grave-name = Give your own name
omen-nameless_grave-dig = Dig it up
omen-nameless_grave-pass = Walk on
omen-nameless_grave = The Nameless Grave
omen-nameless_grave-text = The stone is smooth, without a single mark. The earth beneath it breathes. Whoever lies here needs only a name: any name, even yours.
omen-shadow_market-relic = Buy a curio
omen-shadow_market-potion = Buy a vial
omen-shadow_market-memory = Sell a memory
omen-shadow_market = The Shadow Market
omen-shadow_market-text = They trade in silence and without faces. The goods are real. They take gold, and from those who have none, something they will not remember having.
omen-sleeping_host-watch = Stand the watch
omen-sleeping_host-on = Go on without sleep
omen-sleeping_host = The Sleeping Host
omen-sleeping_host-text = Warriors lie in rows, shield to shield, and they breathe. One could sleep here too, if one of you keeps awake and does not let the host wake.
omen-two_fires-white = To the white fire
omen-two_fires-black = To the black fire
omen-two_fires = Two Fires
omen-two_fires-text = Two fires burn on either side of the trail, one white, one black. At each someone sits with their back to you and shifts over to make room.
omen-gamayun-road = Ask about the road
omen-gamayun-death = Ask about your own death
omen-gamayun-nothing = Ask nothing
omen-gamayun = The Gamayun
omen-gamayun-text = The bird with a woman's face answers one question, and only truly. Those who asked too much still sit around the tree.
omen-last_candle-carry = Carry the candle
omen-last_candle-dark = Walk in the dark
omen-last_candle = The Last Candle
omen-last_candle-text = Beyond here it is dark enough to put out thought. A candle stub stands on a stone. It lights the way for all, but whoever carries it sees their own things in the flame.
omen-sacrifice-hint = A sacrifice: one pays, all gain. Whoever dares first is the one who pays.
omen-schism-hint = A schism: you may not all take the same way.
fx-run-all = Everyone:
fx-run-lose-maxhp = −{ $n } max HP.
error-MustSplit = The others went that way already: yours is the other one
trophy-title = The Trophy
trophy-hint = Each to their own: take one of your three relics.
trophy-waiting = Waiting for: { $who }
chest-title = The Chest
chest-hint = A relic for everyone. Claim yours; if two reach for the same one, rock-paper-scissors settles it.
chest-throw = A dispute! Throw your hand.
chest-thrown = Hand thrown. Waiting for the others…
chest-watch = The others are fighting over a relic.
chest-draw = A draw — again!
chest-shared = The chest is shared out. The losers took the relics nobody claimed.
chest-rock = Rock
chest-paper = Paper
chest-scissors = Scissors
chest-onward = Onward
chest-out = Out: { $who }
building-graveyard = The Graveyard
building-graveyard-desc = Opens the Chronicle: a bestiary of the unclean things you have met, and the memory of past runs.
chronicle-open = Chronicle
chronicle-title = The Graveyard Chronicle
chronicle-met = Unclean things: { $n } of { $all } met
chronicle-runs = Runs: { $runs }  ·  wins: { $wins }
chronicle-won = { $hero } walked out of Nav at dawn  ·  Circle { $circle }
chronicle-fell = { $hero } fell in act { $act } after { $floors } floors  ·  Circle { $circle }
chronicle-analytics = Balance Analytics
building-shrine = The Shrine
building-shrine-desc = In the lobby you may pick another starting relic for your hero: one more per level.
building-palisade = The Palisade
building-palisade-desc = The stockade is rebuilt before your eyes. It changes nothing in a run.

settings-narrator = Storyteller
settings-voices = Spoken lines
settings-voice-lang = Voice
settings-voice-lang-0 = as the text
settings-voice-lang-1 = Old Russian
settings-voice-lang-2 = Russian
settings-voice-lang-3 = English
battle-blocked = Blocked!

hero-bogatyr-desc = The party's shield. Takes the blows meant for others, gathers Valor from the damage he soaks and spends it on crushing finishers.
hero-vorozheya-desc = Lays curses: Rot, Evil Eye and Muted. Her Echo cards devour the foe's curses for power.
hero-volhv-desc = Carves runes on himself and his allies: thunder, frost and mist. Runes fire every turn, and an invocation wakes them all at once.
hero-volkolak-desc = Lives by the Moon. As a man he is quick and hard to hit, as a beast he tears the foe apart; when he turns, his whole hand flips.
hero-znaharka-desc = Gathers herbs in her Cauldron and brews them by recipe: healing the party, poisoning foes, steeling allies.
hero-skomoroh-desc = Wears the masks of Bear, Goat and Mara, confuses the enemy and echoes the cards of others. Strongest beside the party.
